angle shown below under the action of $\\mathbf T.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/853fd7d5c09944a5bacd0c2b3453504f3fa1eea9d8d3b2c3bdd4f0f44889dc16.png)" 13194139535324 true] [17592186105384 1145 "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/95c80fe2654c8f6eb4b65492eab1efb07f568375b2960b1633e5e2e1a7741a8b.png)\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(3,-6), (1,-2),$ and $(-2,4).$  Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/3fd1073b2eaa5aa9c21e537fcc4dc6cf538ab2992c0732f64da50dbcb63d8fd4.png)" 13194139535324 true] [17592186105384 1145 "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(3,-6), (1,-2),$ and $(-2,4).$  Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/3fd1073b2eaa5aa9c21e537fcc4dc6cf538ab2992c0732f64da50dbcb63d8fd4.png)" 13194139535324 false] [17592186105385 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/89efcd0ecb51dac08a1102c5a347eea3459f7209de7cbac0a88b192259ca3b7e.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/501ab476f0e420892fee6c87307dd33f260affc1533019621b366b5462920322.png)\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $\\mathbf{T}?$" 13194139535324 true] [17592186105385 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/89efcd0ecb51dac08a1102c5a347eea3459f7209de7cbac0a88b192259ca3b7e.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $\\mathbf{T}?$" 13194139535324 false] [17592186105818 1020 #edb/ref 17592186343746 13194139535324 true] [17592186105818 1020 #edb/ref 17592186343760 13194139535324 true] [17592186105819 1020 #edb/ref 17592186343739 13194139535324 true] [17592186105819 1020 #edb/ref 17592186343767 13194139535324 true] [17592186105820 1020 #edb/ref 17592186343753 13194139535324 true] [17592186105994 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/e6d0ce147aec90c3840a893e36596fbadf981ff96559f65d055f4486406cca7f.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the quadrilateral shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139535324 true] [17592186105994 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/e6d0ce147aec90c3840a893e36596fbadf981ff96559f65d055f4486406cca7f.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the quadrilateral shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139535324 false] [17592186106081 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/5c0196b13b3f20ba05313a9604e73b13251937b525a12fd5b9997e99f4ae21a0.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139535324 true] [17592186106081 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/5c0196b13b3f20ba05313a9604e73b13251937b525a12fd5b9997e99f4ae21a0.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139535324 false] [17592186106081 1145 "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-1,1)$, $(1,-1),$ $(-1,1).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/2f8d6ec6c9a71e61180ad04c25d623c40dadfdd623e1e2eaa8458915bcaca2f8.png)" 13194139535324 true] [17592186106081 1145 "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-1,1)$, $(1,-1),$ $(-1,1).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/2f8d6ec6c9a71e61180ad04c25d623c40dadfdd623e1e2eaa8458915bcaca2f8.png)" 13194139535324 false] [17592186106471 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535324 true] [17592186106471 1100 "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0, 1)$, $(2, 1)$ and $(1, 0)$. Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of $S^{′}$, the image of $S$ under the action of $T$?\n\n1. $(-2, 1)$\n2. $(-8, 4)$\n3. $(3, 6)$" 13194139535324 false] [17592186106471 1100 "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,1)$, $(2,1)$ and $(1,0).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\n- $(-2,1)$\n- $(-8,4)$\n- $(3,6)$" 13194139535324 true] [17592186106471 1145 "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-8,4)$, $(-12,6)$ and $(-2,1).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139535324 true] [17592186284103 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/57941a3ed467617de9d41a2d8239b75060ba90b7a8c8980e5dabd3afb0be8b6b.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139535324 true] [17592186284103 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/57941a3ed467617de9d41a2d8239b75060ba90b7a8c8980e5dabd3afb0be8b6b.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139535324 false] [17592186284103 1145 "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing 