nce/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/f9040d78661e0d33290ad14e1ddf815211985f5963c8e1c8b9b5438dd8f3931c.png" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343742 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535324 true] [17592186343742 1111 #uuid "98241003-60bb-5256-b8be-25f52dba3b8e" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343743 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/d271c5f4cf0f250dcfdbba8addfdc5f8c583832f378756fc3066e2b961a31dc3.png" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343743 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535324 true] [17592186343743 1111 #uuid "66332007-7e3f-53db-8605-325253d0b6c7" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343744 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/9c045d6467a91676cd27a4c11cbb651a798b2480662d09b446b52d8eeb490ff4.png" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343744 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535324 true] [17592186343744 1111 #uuid "696e8632-6643-5ece-8ded-773adbd5981c" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343745 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/d38c8f370e25add2a06ecc652127bae817e2c8bc394f4db6fdf539fbfef3750c.png" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343745 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535324 true] [17592186343745 1111 #uuid "a774dc82-cfa2-59b4-b4d9-952453262bc5" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343746 1017 #edb/ref 17592186343747 13194139535324 true] [17592186343746 1089 "q-147666" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343746 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535324 true] [17592186343746 1100 "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,3)$, $(-2,0)$ and $(2,-1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\n- $(8,-16)$\n- $(-6,12)$\n- $(8,16)$" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343746 1113 #uuid "ffc47857-8ce0-5ccc-b30b-08427af12d9a" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343746 1145 "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 6 & 12 & -16\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-3,6)$, $(-6,12)$ and $(8,-16).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343747 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343748 13194139535324 true] [17592186343747 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343749 13194139535324 true] [17592186343747 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343750 13194139535324 true] [17592186343747 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343751 13194139535324 true] [17592186343747 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343752 13194139535324 true] [17592186343747 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535324 true] [17592186343747 1041 "selection" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343747 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343751 13194139535324 true] [17592186343747 1110 #uuid "159a3879-ed68-531e-90f5-175d25fe9130" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343748 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343748 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535324 true] [17592186343748 1111 #uuid "6e38b448-a4f1-5259-a3dd-0ca74d634870" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343749 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343749 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535324 true] [17592186343749 1111 #uuid "6d52a694-e1ee-5698-b164-d4305f9af7a2" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343750 1034 "I only" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343750 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535324 true] [17592186343750 1111 #uuid "25f5e060-33c0-51f5-8d38-00ab8a4e4bf8" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343751 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343751 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535324 true] [17592186343751 1111 #uuid "9904973b-0a73-5d3e-ad49-b2ce055d8f57" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343752 1034 "II only" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343752 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535324 true] [17592186343752 1111 #uuid "c035eb50-b3ee-5924-86b0-17822efd0914" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343753 1017 #edb/ref 17592186343754 13194139535324 true] [17592186343753 1089 "q-162203" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343753 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535324 true] [17592186343753 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/bfbd80c4e052ae3c286d25b2cd7bf5a1ffcd76ac5a030b7f9b633d0f12517231.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the pentagon shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343753 1113 #uuid "ec7f25ec-c53e-5db0-8670-17fbf89adc9c" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343753 1145 "Recall that for any linear transformation $T$ with associated $2\\times 2$ matrix $T,$ we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., $det(T)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., $det(T)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $T$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $T$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is the point $(0,0),$ the origin of the coordinate system.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our transformation.\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 9\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot 9-6\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a singular nonzero matrix. Therefore, the image of the pentagon under the action of $T$ is a line segment." 13194139535324 true] [17592186343754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343755 13194139535324 true] [17592186343754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343756 13194139535324 true] [17592186343754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343757 13194139535324 true] [17592186343754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343758 13194139535324 true] [17592186343754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343759 13194139535324 true] [17592186343754 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535324 true] [17592186343754 1041 "selection" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343754 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343758 13194139535324 true] [17592186343754 1110 #uuid "8eb7c053-b2bf-547a-a46c-df87d98b946f" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343755 1034 "The origin $O$ of the coordinate system" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343755 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535324 true] [17592186343755 1111 #uuid "ec42bf66-f144-51df-9408-97d76dbc5561" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343756 1034 "A rectangle" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343756 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535324 true] [17592186343756 1111 #uuid "d115ee20-9dda-513b-9aed-4624b6734666" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343757 1034 "A pentagon" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343757 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535324 true] [17592186343757 1111 #uuid "1de74d72-127e-556b-8427-6d9364d48054" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343758 1034 "A line segment" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343758 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535324 true] [17592186343758 1111 #uuid "099e2f87-23cd-5617-9b1a-dd2d77f75d3f" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343759 1034 "A point, different from the origin" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343759 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535324 true] [17592186343759 1111 #uuid "9274fb24-d9f8-5683-9c48-c7c8265f0645" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343760 1017 #edb/ref 17592186343761 13194139535324 true] [17592186343760 1089 "q-96855" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343760 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535324 true] [17592186343760 1100 "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,-1)$, $(1,0)$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$ \n\n- $(10,20)$\n- $(4,-8)$\n- $(-6,6)$" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343760 1113 #uuid "ce8c6e00-4237-5ad5-a1a9-9c084424d69f" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343760 1145 "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -4 & 10 \\\\ -12 & -8 & 20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-6,-12)$, $(-4,-8)$ and $(10,20).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I  only.\"" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343761 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343762 13194139535324 true] [17592186343761 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343763 13194139535324 true] [17592186343761 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343764 13194139535324 true] [17592186343761 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343765 13194139535324 true] [17592186343761 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343766 13194139535324 true] [17592186343761 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535324 true] [17592186343761 1041 "selection" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343761 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343764 13194139535324 true] [17592186343761 1110 #uuid "dcbb4b71-aa9c-5e19-a4f8-b6f3623f31c2" 13194139535324 true] [17592186343762 1034 "II and III only" 131941